  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Proactive Pangolin Protection: Building Law Enforcement and Community Capacity to Reduce the Pangolin Trade in Nepal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this project is to counter wildlife trafficking in Nepal, with a focus on the highest need areas of Kavrepalanchok and Sankhuwasabha districts, by reducing the number of critically endangered pangolins being illegally removed from the wild for the illegal wildlife trade. This project is intended to conserve Indian pangolins and Chinese pangolins by addressing the impacts of low awareness of, and capacity to act on, the threat to pangolins both within local communities and law enforcement agencies. Specific activities include: (1) mobilizing two community-based anti-poaching units (CBAPUs) in the two districts; (2) raising awareness of pangolin conservation needs and their legal status with local communities in the two districts; and (3) building the capacity of national law enforcement agencies to effectively combat the illegal wildlife trade in pangolins and their body parts..&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
